# The variant-case-payload route of the same defect — its own file, because the
# build stops at the first refusal (panel 067 F8: a case carried three lines
# that proved nothing for months, because an earlier line stopped the build).
#
# This is the shape a per-shape enumeration would have missed, and the reason
# the gate walks transitively rather than checking a list: the `ptr` is not a
# field of a record, it is the payload of a variant case. Symptom, cause and
# fix are in `fixedbugs-pointer-reached-through-a-field.hero`, 2026-08-16,
# panel 068.

extern "stdlib.h"
    function malloc(size: u64) -> ptr

variant Handle
    none
    live
        p: ptr

function main()
    h: Handle @ .live(p: malloc(size: 8))
    by_handle: {Handle: i64} @ {}  #~ pointer_element
    by_handle[h] @ 1
    print(len(by_handle))
